{"t":"2026-11-22T23:22:13.919Z","i":11,"do":"waitReply","expect":"a long answer streams in; it is readable, not cut off, and the buttons under it never cover the words","timeline":[{"at":44,"badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":true,"streaming":0},{"at":5434,"badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":false,"streaming":1},{"at":12555,"badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":false,"streaming":0}],"watchShots":[{"at":1752,"mark":1500,"shot":"21-long-wait-1.5s.png","badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":true,"streaming":0},{"at":3249,"mark":3000,"shot":"22-long-wait-3.0s.png","badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":true,"streaming":0},{"at":6020,"mark":6000,"shot":"23-long-wait-6.0s.png","badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":false,"streaming":1}],"firstReplyMs":5404,"newBubbles":1,"reactions":[],"ok":true,"duplicates":0,"lastReply":"Here is your story: Sheru the tiger and his first biryani.\n\nDeep in the Sundarbans lived a tiger named Sheru who was tired of the same old dinner. One evening a warm, spicy smell drifted in from a village wedding across the river, and he followed it to a giant pot of biryani. He hid behind a banyan tree and watched the old cook, Rahim Chacha, layer rice and masala like he was tucking a baby into bed. Sheru decided that night he would learn to make it himself.\n\nHis first tries were a disaster. He burnt the onions, dropped a whole fistful of chillies in the pot and sneezed so hard the monkeys fell out of their trees laughing. The rice came out as mush one day and as pebbles the next. But Sheru went back to the banyan tree every evening, and slowly learned the secrets: fry the onions slow and golden, soak the rice first, and never lift the lid while it is on dum.\n\nOn the night of the full moon, Sheru finally opened his pot, and the smell floated through the whole jungle. Deer, monkeys and even the grumpy old crocodile lined up with banana-leaf plates, a little nervous about the chef. Sheru served every one of them with a proud grin and took the last helping for himself. From then on, nobody in the jungle feared the tiger's roar, only the day his biryani ran out. 🐯\n\n4:52 AM","kit":[],"replyFaults":[],"ms":18624,"shot":"24-long.png"}
